NAME
       lscpu - show information about the processors

SYNOPSIS
       lscpu

DESCRIPTION
       lscpu prints the processor architecture (x86_64), the number of CPUs
       and how they are arranged (sockets, cores per socket, threads per
       core), the model name, the virtualisation it sees, and the cache
       sizes. nproc prints just the number of CPUs; /proc/cpuinfo has the
       raw details.

       The number of CPUs helps to read the load average in uptime and top: a
       load of 2.0 is full use on two CPUs but only half on four.

EXAMPLES
           lscpu
           lscpu | grep '^CPU(s)'

SEE ALSO
       nproc(1), uptime(1), top(1)
